---
description: Architecture practices for React and Next.js with the App Router.
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only when the component needs state, effects, or browser interactions.
- Keep presentation, interaction logic, and data access separate, following the project's conventions.
- Do not turn a component into a client component only to use a hook when the logic can be resolved on the server.
- Prefer passing data from the server into client components over repeating requests or moving logic to the browser without need.
- Use Server Actions for write operations when that matches the project pattern. Centralize queries and mutations through the existing data-access layers.
- Validate every received value on the server and apply the required authorization checks. Never rely only on client-side validation.
- Avoid duplicate requests, unnecessary cascades, and data waterfalls. Use Next.js rendering, cache, and revalidation only for a real need.
- Respect the server and client boundary. Never expose secrets or server-only code to the browser.
